# Todoer needs none of these: with nothing set, its setup screens connect
# your Supabase project and keep the keys in the app-data folder (README,
# "Connect Supabase"). Set them only to give the project another way, for
# example on a host with no setup screens. Copy this file to .env.local.
# Next reads it when Todoer starts, and git ignores it.

# ─── Your Supabase project ───────────────────────────────────────────
# All three, or Todoer names the ones missing. The secret key never reaches
# the browser: Todoer reads it on the server only.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://abcdefghijklmnopqrst.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...

# ─── Where Todoer keeps its settings ─────────────────────────────────
# Instead of ~/Library/Application Support/Todoer, %LOCALAPPDATA%\Todoer
# or ~/.config/todoer. `npm run develop` sets it to .dev-data.
# TODOER_DATA_DIR=

# ─── Ramble ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A Groq key, used when none is saved in Settings.
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
# A publik key and its address, instead of the one Settings sets up.
# PUBLIK_API_KEY=pk_...
# PUBLIK_API_BASE_URL=https://publikhq.com/api/v1
